## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | js/unit-tests/test_mergeBot.js | ⚠️ important the new dedup in mergebot rollupdetail has no test — and latestentries has no direct unit tests the merge gate s evidence ladder is pinned branch by branch by the characterization suite its own header a silent shape change would starve or force merges and this pr inserts a new step into exactly that ladder js return combinerunstates mergestatereconcile latestentries runs map deciderunstate test mergebot js only adds the require mapping this line — no test exercises rollupdetail with duplicate check run names so a regression in the wiring wrong helper wrong argument order dedup dropped would silently force or starve merges with the whole suite green same for latestentries itself test mergestatereconcile js 63 tests is untouched the only coverage is the indirect happy path via the new prstatus test named duplicates with timestamps untested branches of the new helper anonymous name context less entries staying in the tally the id position tie breaks and first appearance order preservation — all behavior failingchecknames combinerunstates consumers now inherit per agents md all new js logic must be covered by unit tests before committing please add 1 a rollupdetail characterization test check runs failure quality gate t1 success quality gate t2 → green and the inverse pin the older entry must win when its timestamp is newer 2 direct latestentries tests in test mergestatereconcile js for anon pasthrough id tie break and stable ordering |
| F2 | open | SUGGESTION | js/common/mergeStateReconcile.js | 💡 suggestion a queued re run carries no timestamp and loses to the older failure — the poison window survives the queued phase sorttimeof reads only completed at completedat started at startedat and a queued check run has neither — it degrades to t 0 js var t sorttimeof r queued re run → date parse 0 so when an in place re run of a failed job creates a fresh check run in queued state no completed at and started at only once it actually begins the older failure entry t1 0 wins the latestentries collapse and the head keeps reading red until the re run enters in progress that is exactly the fa 236 poison narrowed to the queued phase rather than removed — pre fix behavior also read red there so this is no regression but please confirm against the api shape you see on dispatched re runs if queued check runs can arrive with started at null consider falling back to created at or to run id position when timestamps tie at 0 so a queued re run immediately supersedes the older conclusion the way github branch protection treats it if dispatched re runs always carry started at from creation this is moot — a comment saying so on the helper would close the question |
| F3 | open | SUGGESTION | js/sm/validationCheckSync.js | 💡 suggestion dispatched run arming is unbounded — and now also arms prs the machine never managed two clarity points on the broadened predicate the feature itself is sound and matches the pr intent 1 unbounded restamp loop label based arming ended when the machine swapped ai validating validation failed away this match ignores labels entirely so an open pr whose head carries a workflow dispatch run of ciworkflow stays armed for the life of the head — and syncsinglearmedpr posts fresh umbrella check runs every eligible tick each stamp is a new check run — checkrunstamp is a post not a patch until the pr merges closes or pushes a new head for a pr that lingers open waiting on human review that is a perpetual write loop consider skipping the stamp when the newest existing umbrella check run already carries the same verdict — the latestentries work in this pr is exactly what makes repeated stamps verdict safe so a same verdict short circuit would keep the rescue behavior at one stamp per verdict change 2 human dispatched runs arm too any manual run workflow of ciworkflow on any open pr head now triggers machine authored umbrella stamps on that pr that is arguably intended sync umbrella checks on dispatched heads but it deserves a one line comment on this predicate saying manual dispatches are in scope so a future reader doesn t treat it as a bug neither blocks the stamps faithfully mirror the dispatched run s conclusion and fa 236 s rescue window is transient in the happy path |
| F4 | open | SUGGESTION | js/common/smProvider.js | 🪶 nit dead defensive fallback silently disables the fix mergestatereconcile is a top level require smprovider js 193 and latestentries ships in the same pack closure so the guard can never be false in a consistent build js var deduped mergestatereconcile latestentries mergestatereconcile latestentries rollup rollup if it ever did evaluate falsy partial stub stale module dedup would silently turn off — the one behavior this pr exists to restore — with no log line a direct call var deduped mergestatereconcile latestentries rollup fails loudly instead of quietly reverting to the poisoned tally no behavioral impact today pure robustness preference |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

# PR new hunks — what changed since the last review concluded

Last reviewed head: f5871bfd2222f75fc0a8e54921294dfa3a4e15ee
Current head: 01e60adb304ad7836a3fd45e1b4e98b65ab8b36d

These hunks are the re-review scope, together with their interaction
neighborhood (direct callers/callees of changed symbols). Every line
NOT shown here is frozen: a finding on an unchanged line must show that
these hunks make the problem worse (the interaction test) — otherwise
it is advisory digest only, never a review thread.

--- diff ---

diff --git a/js/common/mergeStateReconcile.js b/js/common/mergeStateReconcile.js
index 82252ed717..02e98ceaec 100644
--- a/js/common/mergeStateReconcile.js
+++ b/js/common/mergeStateReconcile.js
@@ -172,6 +172,8 @@ function latestConclusions(rollup) {
 /**
  * Collapse multiple check-runs per context name to the LATEST entry (#695
  * branch-protection semantics) while keeping anonymous entries intact.
+ * Note: GitHub stamps started_at on check-run creation (including queued
